# No clear winner: it's close

No car came out on top often enough to call it. The leader won in only **52%** of the simulated futures, a lead of 4% over the runner-up.

## Genuinely close

No single factor changes which car leads. Over 5 years these cars cost you about the same once your preferences are counted, so you can choose on anything the numbers don't capture: test drives, dealer, looks. That is a useful answer, not a failure.

